From a097ceada709b6b6d6c26da9358d26fe7e34ef81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:28:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/timer: TCC model, checked against PIC32CM MC00 silicon

TCC U2213: counting from GCLK_TCC through the prescaler in the single-
slope (NFRQ, MFRQ, NPWM) and dual-slope waveform modes with the
instance's counter width, overflow and compare-match flags, the waveform
output state in STATUS.CMPx, one-shot, the commands, double buffering,
the counter event selection (CNTSEL) and the events: OVF, TRG, CNT, MCx
out; RETRIGGER, COUNTEV, START, INC, COUNT, DIR, STOP, DEC in. Event
driven on QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL with closed-form jumps over ticks that
change nothing.

Behaviour the data sheet leaves open or gets wrong follows silicon
(firmware/hello/tests/tccprobe.c): where MCx and CMPx change, the dual-
slope direction, buffer writes holding SYNCBUSY until the copy, STOP
clearing COUNT, COUNTEV/INC replacing the clock, the CNT rules.

New qtest pic32cm-tcc-test; board docs list the TCC.

Peripheral Pretender: a personal project; not for upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
